-- lib/pool.cub — the laws of the served source (src/syntax.c, the view; lib/host.cub and lib/server.cub,
-- the exchange; Avik, 2026-11-17: "There is no canonical state"). A pool is the set of objects it holds:
-- its membership, an object's being held. Two pools meet by union. What a pool holds at a path follows
-- from its membership alone: an entry is live when the pool holds it and holds no entry that follows
-- it (replaces it, or states it dead). Proven here: union is commutative, associative and idempotent,
-- so pools that send each other what the other lacks, in any order and any number of times, come to
-- hold the same; and the view depends on nothing but the membership, so two pools holding the same
-- entries hold the same view, whatever order they took them in.
import "core.cub"
